-- title:
--   Cube-free saturation forces equal levels and identical Hecke localisations
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a characteristic-zero discrete valuation domain, complete for the adic topology of its maximal ideal and with finite residue field $k=\mathrm{ResidueField}\,\mathcal O$, let $p$ be a prime with $p\neq 2$ whose image lies in the maximal ideal of $\mathcal O$, and let $\bar\rho$ be a residual Galois representation over $k$, that is a $2$-dimensional $k$-space with an action of $\mathrm{Aut}_{\mathbb Q}(\overline{\mathbb Q})$ trivial on the absolute Galois group of some finite subextension, assumed irreducible in the sense that every Galois-stable $k$-subspace is $\bot$ or $\top$. Let $S$ be a finite set of primes containing $p$, and let $M\mid M'$ be nonzero levels all of whose prime divisors lie in $S$, subject to: for every prime $q\mid M'$ with $q\neq p$, either $q^2\mid M$ or $q^n\mid M'$ implies $q^n\mid M$ for all $n$; $q^3\nmid M'$ for every prime $q\neq p$; $p^k\mid M'$ implies $p^k\mid M$; and at every prime $q\mid M'$ with $q\neq p$ either $\bar\rho$ is unramified at $q$ (inertia at every valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lying over $q$ acts trivially) or the associated adic representation has characteristic polynomial $(X-1)^2$ on all such inertia elements. Assume furthermore that the spaces $S_2(\Gamma_0(M))$ and $S_2(\Gamma_0(M'))$ are spanned over $\mathbb C$ by their submodules of forms with integral $q$-expansions. Let $\theta$ and $\theta'$ be ring homomorphisms to $k$ from the anemic Hecke algebras at levels $M$ and $M'$, the $\mathbb Z$-subalgebras of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb C}$ of weight-$2$ cusp forms generated by the $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell\notin S$ not dividing the level together with the $U_q$ for primes $q\notin S$ dividing it, such that $\theta'(T_\ell)=\theta(T_\ell)$ for all primes $\ell\nmid M'$, $\ell\notin S$, and such that for all primes $\ell\nmid M$, $\ell\notin S$, every valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ over $\ell$ and every $\sigma$ which is a Frobenius at $\ell$ for $P$ one has $\mathrm{charpoly}(\bar\rho(\sigma))=X^2-\theta(T_\ell)X+\ell$. The conclusion asserts the existence of an isomorphism $e$ of $\mathcal O$-algebras from [`CuspForm.heckeLocal`](def/CuspForm_HeckeLocal.html#L131) at level $M'$ for $\theta'$ to [`CuspForm.heckeLocal`](def/CuspForm_HeckeLocal.html#L131) at level $M$ for $\theta$ — the localisations of the $\mathcal O$-base changes of the two Hecke algebras at the multiplicative sets coming from the complements of the primes attached to $\theta'$ and $\theta$ — such that $e$ carries the image under the canonical map [`CuspForm.heckeLocal.π`](def/CuspForm_HeckeLocal.html#L151) of $T_\ell$ at level $M'$ to the image of $T_\ell$ at level $M$, for every prime $\ell\notin S$ with $\ell\nmid M'$.
--
--   This is the level-comparison step of the argument, asserting that passing from a level $M'$ to a divisor $M$ satisfying the stated saturation, cube-freeness, equal $p$-part and semistable-type conditions induces an isomorphism of the $\theta$-localised anemic Hecke algebras matching the Hecke operators away from $S$. It is used in the computation of newform multiplicities, where the finrank of an intersection of eigenspaces over the algebraic closure is identified for corner realisations with no cube dividing the level.
